{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_011","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"Events Ambassadors Developer Funding XRPL Jobs Dev Blog XRPL Grants GitHub Report a Scam","location_hint":"paragraph 32","char_start":752,"char_end":840,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_012","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"Copy page as Markdown for LLMs","location_hint":"paragraph 73","char_start":1604,"char_end":1634,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_013","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The NFToken object represents a single non-fungible token (NFT). It is not stored on its own, but is contained in a NFTokenPage object alongside other NFToken objects.","location_hint":"paragraph 84","char_start":1892,"char_end":2059,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_014","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"Requires the NonFungibleTokensV1_1 amendment . Loading...","location_hint":"paragraph 85","char_start":2061,"char_end":2118,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_015","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"{\n\"NFTokenID\" : \"000B013A95F14B0044F78A264E41713C64B5F89242540EE208C3098E00000D65\" ,\n\"URI\" : \"ipfs://bafybeigdyrzt5sfp7udm7hu76uh7y26nf4dfuylqabf3oclgtqy55fbzdi\"\n}","location_hint":"paragraph 87","char_start":2146,"char_end":2309,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_016","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"Unlike full-fledged ledger entries , NFToken has no field to identify the object type or current owner of the object. NFToken objects are grouped into pages that implicitly define the object type and identify the owner.","location_hint":"paragraph 88","char_start":2311,"char_end":2530,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_017","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"NFTokenID , optional, string, UInt256","location_hint":"paragraph 90","char_start":2543,"char_end":2580,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_018","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"This composite field uniquely identifies a token, and consists of the following sections.","location_hint":"paragraph 91","char_start":2582,"char_end":2671,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_019","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"A) 16 bits that identify flags or settings specific to the NFToken","location_hint":"paragraph 92","char_start":2673,"char_end":2739,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_020","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"B) 16 bits that encode the transfer fee associated with this NFToken, if any","location_hint":"paragraph 93","char_start":2741,"char_end":2817,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_021","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"C) A 160-bit account identifier of the issuer","location_hint":"paragraph 94","char_start":2819,"char_end":2864,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_022","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"D) A 32-bit issuer-specified NFTokenTaxon","location_hint":"paragraph 95","char_start":2866,"char_end":2907,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_023","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"E) An (automatically generated) monotonically increasing 32-bit sequence number.","location_hint":"paragraph 96","char_start":2909,"char_end":2989,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_024","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The 16-bit flags, transfer fee fields, the 32-bit NFTokenTaxon , and the sequence number fields are stored in big-endian format.","location_hint":"paragraph 97","char_start":2993,"char_end":3121,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_025","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"Flags are properties or other options associated with the NFToken object.","location_hint":"paragraph 99","char_start":3138,"char_end":3211,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_026","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"Flag Name Flag Value Description","location_hint":"paragraph 100","char_start":3215,"char_end":3247,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_027","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"lsfBurnable 0x0001 If enabled, the issuer (or an entity authorized by the issuer) can destroy this NFToken . The object&#x27;s owner can always do so.","location_hint":"paragraph 101","char_start":3251,"char_end":3401,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_028","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"lsfOnlyXRP 0x0002 If enabled, this NFToken can only be offered or sold for XRP.","location_hint":"paragraph 102","char_start":3403,"char_end":3482,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_029","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"lsfTrustLine 0x0004 DEPRECATED If enabled, automatically create trust lines to hold transfer fees. Otherwise, buying or selling this NFToken for a fungible token amount fails if the issuer does not have a trust line for that token. The fixRemoveNFTokenAutoTrustLine amendment makes it invalid to enable this flag.","location_hint":"paragraph 103","char_start":3484,"char_end":3797,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_030","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"lsfTransferable 0x0008 If enabled, this NFToken can be transferred from one holder to another. Otherwise, it can only be transferred to or from the issuer.","location_hint":"paragraph 104","char_start":3799,"char_end":3954,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_031","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"lsfReservedFlag 0x8000 This flag is reserved for future use. Attempts to set this flag fail.","location_hint":"paragraph 105","char_start":3956,"char_end":4048,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_032","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"lsfMutable 0x0010 If enabled, the URI field of the NFToken can be updated using the NFTokenModify transaction.","location_hint":"paragraph 106","char_start":4050,"char_end":4160,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_033","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"NFToken flags are immutable: they can only be set during the NFTokenMint transaction and cannot be changed later.","location_hint":"paragraph 107","char_start":4164,"char_end":4277,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_034","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The example sets three flags: lsfBurnable ( 0x0001 ), lsfOnlyXRP ( 0x0002 ), lsfTransferable ( 0x0008 ). 1+2+8 = 11, or 0x000B in big endian format.","location_hint":"paragraph 109","char_start":4288,"char_end":4436,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_035","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The TransferFee value specifies the percentage fee, in units of 1/100,000, charged by the issuer for secondary sales of the token. Valid values for this field are between 0 and 50,000, inclusive. A value of 1 is equivalent to 0.001% or 1/10 of a basis point (bps), allowing transfer rates between 0% and 50%.","location_hint":"paragraph 111","char_start":4453,"char_end":4761,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_036","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"This value sets the transfer fee to 314, or 0.314%.","location_hint":"paragraph 113","char_start":4772,"char_end":4823,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_037","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The third section of the NFTokenID is a big endian representation of the issuer’s public address.","location_hint":"paragraph 115","char_start":4850,"char_end":4947,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_038","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The fourth section is a NFTokenTaxon created by the issuer.","location_hint":"paragraph 117","char_start":4965,"char_end":5024,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_039","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"An issuer might issue several NFToken objects with the same NFTokenTaxon ; to ensure that NFToken objects are spread across multiple pages, the NFTokenTaxon is scrambled using the fifth section, a sequential number, as the seed for a random number generator. The scrambled value is stored with the NFToken , but the unscrambled value is the actual NFTokenTaxon .","location_hint":"paragraph 118","char_start":5028,"char_end":5390,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_040","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"Notice that the scrambled version of the NFTokenTaxon is 0xBC8B858E , the scrambled version of the NFTokenTaxon specified by the issuer. But the actual value of the NFTokenTaxon is the unscrambled value.","location_hint":"paragraph 119","char_start":5392,"char_end":5595,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_041","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The fifth section is a sequence number that increases with each NFToken the issuer creates.","location_hint":"paragraph 121","char_start":5613,"char_end":5704,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_042","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The NFTokenMint transaction sets this part of the NFTokenID automatically based on the MintedNFTokens field of the Issuer account. If the issuer&#x27;s AccountRoot object does not have a MintedNFTokens field, the field is assumed to have the value 0; the value of the field is then incremented by exactly 1.","location_hint":"paragraph 122","char_start":5708,"char_end":6015,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_043","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The URI field points to the data or metadata associated with the NFToken . This field does not need to be an HTTP or HTTPS URL; it could be an IPFS URI, a magnet link, an RFC 2379 \"data\" URL , or even a totally custom encoding. The URI is not checked for validity, but the field is limited to a maximum length of 256 bytes.","location_hint":"paragraph 124","char_start":6022,"char_end":6345,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_044","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The URI is immutable, so no one can update it if, for example, it links to a website that no longer exists.","location_hint":"paragraph 126","char_start":6358,"char_end":6465,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_045","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"Retrieving NFToken Data and Metadata","location_hint":"paragraph 127","char_start":6467,"char_end":6503,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_046","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"To minimize the footprint of NFTokens without sacrificing functionality or imposing unnecessary restrictions, XRPL NFTs do not have arbitrary data fields. Instead, data is maintained separately and referenced by the NFToken . The URI provides a reference to immutable content for the Hash and any mutable data for the NFToken object.","location_hint":"paragraph 128","char_start":6505,"char_end":6838,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_047","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The URI field is especially useful for referring to non-traditional Peer-to-Peer (P2P) URLs. For example, a minter that stores NFToken data or metadata using the Inter Planetary File System (IPFS) can use the URI field to refer to data on IPFS in different ways, each of which is suited to different use-cases. For more context on types of IPFS links that can be used to store NFT data, see Best Practices for Storing NFT Data using IPFS ,","location_hint":"paragraph 129","char_start":6840,"char_end":7279,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_048","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"The format for a text record is as follows.","location_hint":"paragraph 131","char_start":7300,"char_end":7343,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_049","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"xrpl-nft-data-token-info-v1 IN TXT \"https://host.example.com/api/token-info/{nftokenid}\"","location_hint":"paragraph 132","char_start":7349,"char_end":7437,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_050","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"Replace the string {nftokenid} with the requested NFTokenID as a 64-byte hex string when you attempt to query information.","location_hint":"paragraph 133","char_start":7439,"char_end":7561,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_d0882a19791f_051","source_id":"src_d0882a19791f","source_hash":"03e517349f0d76c64337973dddf73d725e26e124f3ba844f8eef6e86b06d739e","text":"Your implementation should check for the presence of TXT records and use those query strings if present. If no string is present, implementations should attempt to use a default URL. Assuming the domain is example.com , the default URL would be:","location_hint":"paragraph 134","char_start":7563,"char_end":7808,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:39:02.150Z"}
